  "result": "CommonJS order utilities: `calcTotal` sums price×qty, `applyDiscount` applies SAVE10/SAVE20 percent codes, `averageItemPrice` divides total by count, `formatOrder` renders line items plus discounted total.\n\nBugs:\n1. `orders.js:5` — off-by-one: `i <= items.length` reads `items[items.length]` (undefined) → TypeError on every call. Should be `i < items.length`.\n2. `orders.js:20` — division by zero on empty `items` → returns `NaN`. Guard with `items.length === 0 ? 0 : …`.\n3. `orders.js:13` — `discounts[code]` inherits `Object.prototype`, so codes like `constructor`/`toString` return a function; `total * pct` then yields `NaN`. Use `Object.hasOwn(discounts, code)` or `Object.create(null)`.",
